{"title":"KVPY","category":"Engineering","bank":"kvpy","subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Matrices","count":5,"questions":[{"id":51725,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Matrices","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> be a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn></math> matrix of the form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>,</mo></math> where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>b</mi></math> are integers and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>.</mo></math> The number of such matrices <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math> the inverse of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo></math> exists and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> contains only integer entries is","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>101</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>202</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mn>101</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></math>"],"answer":2,"solution":"<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo></math></p>\n\n<p>Also, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mn>1</mn></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mstyle></mfrac><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mtable columnalign=\"center center\" columnspacing=\"1em\" rowspacing=\"4pt\"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></msup></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mtable columnalign=\"center center\" columnspacing=\"1em\" rowspacing=\"4pt\"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>−</mo><mi>b</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math><br />\nThus, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>ii</mi></mfenced></math><br />\nSo, required number of pairs <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>b</mi><mo>)</mo></math> is<br />\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>101</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>202</mn></math></p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2020 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"614da75131310175e098011f"},{"id":51726,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Matrices","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"Suppose <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>c</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>d</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math> is a real matrix with non-zero entries, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></math>. Then, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></math> equals","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>"],"answer":0,"solution":"<p>We have,</p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>c</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>d</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>c</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>d</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>c</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>d</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>d</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p>Given, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>d</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mi>d</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>b</mi><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>c</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>d</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>b</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>b</mi></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2018 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"614da6a0a86223cefeb08562"},{"id":51727,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Matrices","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"Let $P$ be an $m \\times m$ matrix such that $P^{2}=P$. Then $(1+P)^{n}$ equals -","options":["$I+P$","$I+n P$","$I+2^{n} P$","$I+\\left(2^{n}-1\\right) P$"],"answer":3,"solution":"$\\begin{array}{l}\\mathrm{P}^{2}=\\mathrm{P} \\\\ \\mathrm{P}^{-1} \\mathrm{P}^{2}=\\mathrm{P}^{-1} \\mathrm{P} \\\\ \\mathrm{P}=\\mathrm{I} \\\\ (\\mathrm{I}+\\mathrm{P})^{\\mathrm{n}}=(2 \\mathrm{P})^{\\mathrm{n}}=2^{\\mathrm{n}} \\mathrm{P}^{\\mathrm{n}}\\end{array}\n$=2^{n} \\mathrm{P}=\\mathrm{P}+\\left(2^{\\mathrm{n}}-1\\right) \\mathrm{P}=\\mathrm{I}+\\left(2^{\\mathrm{n}}-1\\right) \\mathrm{P}","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2011 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d2130274702e2bc9a3c9"},{"id":51728,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Matrices","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"Let A denote the matrix $\\left(\\begin{array}{ll}0 & i \\\\ i & 0\\end{array}\\right)$, where $i^{2}=-1$, and let I denote the identity matrix $\\left(\\begin{array}{ll}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{array}\\right)$. Then $\\mathrm{I}+\\mathrm{A}+\\mathrm{A}^{2}+\\ldots+\\mathrm{A}^{2010} \\mathrm{is}-$","options":["$\\left(\\begin{array}{ll}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right)$","$\\left(\\begin{array}{ll}0 & i \\\\ i & 0\\end{array}\\right)$","$\\left(\\begin{array}{ll}1 & 1 \\\\ \\mathrm{i} & 1\\end{array}\\right)$","$\\left(\\begin{array}{cc}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{array}\\right)$"],"answer":2,"solution":"\n\\begin{array}{l}\n\\mathrm{A}=\\left[\\begin{array}{ll}\n0 & \\mathrm{i} \\\\\n\\mathrm{i} & 0\n\\end{array}\\right] ; \\mathrm{A}^{2}=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc}\n-1 & 0 \\\\\n0 & -1\n\\end{array}\\right] ; \\quad \\mathrm{A}^{3}=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc}\n0 & -\\mathrm{i} \\\\\n-\\mathrm{i} & 0\n\\end{array}\\right] ; \\quad \\mathrm{I}=\\left[\\begin{array}{ll}\n1 & 0 \\\\\n0 & 1\n\\end{array}\\right] \\\\\n\\mathrm{I}+\\mathrm{A}+\\mathrm{A}^{2}+\\mathrm{A}^{3}=\\left[\\begin{array}{ll}\n0 & 0 \\\\\n0 & 0\n\\end{array}\\right] \\quad ; \\quad \\mathrm{A}^{4}=\\left[\\begin{array}{ll}\n1 & 0 \\\\\n0 & 1\n\\end{array}\\right]=\\mathrm{I} \\\\\n\\mathrm{I}+\\mathrm{A}+\\mathrm{A}^{2}+\\mathrm{A}^{3}+\\ldots \\ldots \\mathrm{A}^{210} \\\\\n\\left(\\mathrm{I}+\\mathrm{A}+\\mathrm{A}^{2}+\\mathrm{A}^{3}\\right)+\\mathrm{A}^{4}\\left(\\mathrm{I}+\\mathrm{A}+\\mathrm{A}^{2}+\\mathrm{A}^{3}\\right)+\\ldots+\\mathrm{A}^{2008}\\left(\\mathrm{I}+\\mathrm{A}+\\mathrm{A}^{2}\\right) \\\\\n=\\left(\\begin{array}{ll}\n1 & \\mathrm{i} \\\\\n\\mathrm{i} & 1\n\\end{array}\\right)\n\\end{array}\n","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2010 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d21369faebda8d62907a"},{"id":51729,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Matrices","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><munder><mi>j</mi><mo>¯</mo></munder><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub></math> be a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>3</mn></math> invertible matrix where each <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></math> is a real number. Denote the inverse of the matrix <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>l</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></munderover><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br />\nfor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then","options":["sum of the diagonal entries of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>","sum of each row of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>","sum of each row and each column of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>","sum of the diagonal entries of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>"],"answer":1,"solution":"<p>Sum of elements in each row of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo></math></p>\n\n<p>So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math><br />\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo> </mo><mi>A</mi><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math><br />\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math><br />\n<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo></math> sum of elements in each row of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>A</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math></p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2020 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"614da75179a1a356f840a827"}]}